dialect protocol
protocol stdio.pdf.diff
version 1
schema stdio.pdf.diff
start diff

# P2-FG3: `protocol::DiffCodec::encode_diff`/`decode_diff` for `stdio.pdf` (1.4)'s `PdfDiff` are
# derive-generated (`#[derive(dsl::DslDiff)]`, ../../🦀️component.rs) -- ALREADY real binary before
# this wave touched it, NOT the F6-era `print_diff().into_bytes()` text-as-binary shortcut
# (confirmed empirically, not assumed: a real `[DEBUG]` dump of `encode_diff` starts with the
# exact 8-byte `.spk` magic `[137,83,80,75,13,10,26,10]` = `0x8953504B0D0A1A0A`, matching
# `store::pack_rt::encode_document`'s real container, never `print_diff`). Unlike the sibling
# mutations facet's `OpBinary` (which forwards to the LIGHT `os_pack::encode_record_body` helper),
# `encode_document` wraps the record in the FULL `.spk` document container
# (`🎒️pack/📐️format/🦀️component.rs`) -- a real, checksummed, chunk-table-indexed,
# optionally-deflate-compressed random-access file format, not a lightweight per-message frame.
# This file models the one fixed, ALWAYS-present, self-contained structure: the 24-byte superblock
# header (magic + format version + feature-flag bitfields + a self-CRC over the header, the CRC
# value itself opaque here -- no CRC-verification primitive exists at this dialect layer, same
# "structurally irreducible" treatment M2 gives every other checksum) -- confirmed field-for-field
# against the real dump's own byte layout (`version_major`=1, `version_minor`=0,
# `required_flags`=1 [bit0 REQUIRED_COMPRESSED genuinely set on real diff payloads], `optional_flags`=1,
# a non-zero `header_crc32`, then an 8-byte reserved span, all exactly as below). Every OTHER byte
# (segment table, chunk table, symbol table, the deflate-compressed record body, and an 84-byte
# magic-scanned-backward footer) forms a real random-access, checksum-validated, compressed
# document container -- a framework-level container shared verbatim by every
# `#[derive(dsl::DslDiff)]` type in the whole repo, not `stdio.pdf`-specific (the same gap
# `stdio.txt`'s own identical protocol file documents,
# `txt-diffcodec-spk-container-is-framework-level`, recorded once more here in this wave's
# `mechanism_gaps`). Modeled honestly: the 24-byte header IS genuinely, individually byte-walked
# and validated, field for field; everything past it is one opaque tail.
framing magic 0x8953504B0D0A1A0A
header fixed 24
field version_major u16
field version_minor u16
field required_flags u32
field optional_flags u32
field header_crc32 u32
field reserved fixed 8
chain bytes
